Example configuration:

In OpenDaylight, the OSS system can use the RESTCONF API to send a request to the SDN controller to update the network configuration:
```bash
POST /restconf/config/network-topology:network-topology/topology/topology-netconf:1/topology/node/leaf-1/config HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/yang-data+json

{
  "network-topology:node": {
    "node-id": "leaf-1",
    "termination-point": [
      {
        "tp-id": "1/1/1",
        "tp-config": {
          "interface": {
            "name": "eth1",
            "description": "OSS-assured interface"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
