The `OBJECT-GROUP` construct within MIB modules is used to group related objects together for easier management and monitoring, allowing for the definition of a set of objects that can be accessed or modified as a single unit, while the `NOTIFICATION-GROUP` construct is used to group related notifications together, enabling the definition of a set of notifications that can be sent as a single event, typically for alerting or logging purposes. 

Example of `OBJECT-GROUP` definition in SMIv2 (SNMPv2) MIB module syntax:
```sql
OBJECT-GROUP OBJECTS { sysUpTime, sysContact, sysLocation }
  STATUS current
  DESCRIPTION "A collection of system group objects.";
```
Example of `NOTIFICATION-GROUP` definition in SMIv2 (SNMPv2) MIB module syntax:
```sql
NOTIFICATION-GROUP NOTIFICATIONS { coldStart, warmStart }
  STATUS current
  DESCRIPTION "A collection of cold and warm start notifications.";
```

