A `leaf` in a YANG model represents a single value of a particular type, whereas a `leaf-list` represents a list of values of the same type. In NETCONF XML, a `leaf` is typically represented as a single element, whereas a `leaf-list` is represented as a container with multiple child elements, each containing a single value.

Example:
```xml
<!-- leaf -->
<leaf>value</leaf>

<!-- leaf-list -->
<leaf-list>
  <value>value1</value>
  <value>value2</value>
  <value>value3</value>
</leaf-list>
```
In YANG, the difference is represented in the model definition:
```yang
// leaf
leaf value {
  type string;
}

// leaf-list
leaf-list values {
  type string;
}
```

