To establish a URLLC (Ultra-Reliable and Low-Latency Communication) slice for real-time medical diagnostics in 'Europe-Central', we can use the following ETSI-compliant configuration on a 5G network:

```bash
# Define the URLLC slice profile
gNB-configuration {
  urllc-profile {
    name = "medical-diagnostics";
    latency = 5ms;
    reliability = "high";
    bandwidth = {
      uplink = 100Mbps;
      downlink = 100Mbps;
    }
  }
}

# Create a new slice with the defined URLLC profile
slice {
  name = "medical-diagnostics-europe-central";
  urllc-profile = "medical-diagnostics";
  location = "Europe-Central";
}
```

This configuration defines a URLLC slice with a latency of 5ms, high reliability, and guaranteed bandwidth of 100 Mbps each way, specifically for real-time medical diagnostics in the 'Europe-Central' region.

