data.model_answer_raw:
To provision an eMBB slice for large-scale enterprise data sync in South-America, configure a 5G network slice with the following parameters: 
- Slice Type: eMBB (Enhanced Mobile Broadband)
- Guaranteed Bit Rate (GBR): 500 Mbps (UL) and 5 Gbps (DL)
- Latency: Normal (target latency of 50 ms or less)
- Slice Activation: Activate the slice with a specific 5G cell ID and a dedicated 5G RAN (Radio Access Network) configuration.

Example configuration in a 5G Core network using 3GPP-compliant protocols:
```bash
# Define the eMBB slice
network slice-subscription {
  id: eMBB-Slice-SA;
  description: "eMBB Slice for South America";
  type: eMBB;
  gbr-uplink: 500000 kbps;
  gbr-downlink: 5000000 kbps;
  latency: normal;
}

# Activate the slice with a specific 5G cell ID
network slice-activation {
  id: eMBB-Slice-SA;
  cell-id: 123456;
  ran-configuration {
    rrc-configuration {
      rrc-connection-establishment {
        target-plmn-id: "South America";
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Note: The above configuration is a simplified example and may vary based on the specific 5G network architecture and vendor implementation.

